// Axis delta: depth .glow — a coloured halo, no offset — the accent bleeding off the surface.
//
// Mood-INdependent WITHOUT a cross product, because the ink is bound to a
// token the mood has already solved rather than to a literal. A hard shadow
// in opaque black is invisible on a near-black page — the same ground
// dependence that forced the accent axis into 48 generated files — but
// `l0_text` is by construction the colour that READS on this mood's ground,
// and `l0_accent` is the hue the card asked for. So the shape is stated here
// and the colour is inherited, and one file serves every palette.
// `l0_text`, NOT `l0_accent`, and the difference is the whole value of the
// pixel column in `axis_proof.py`. Bound to the accent, `depth: .glow` on a card
// that names no accent read an undefined token — transparent — so the backend
// fell through to the derived soft shadow and the axis measured 0.08, i.e.
// nothing. It looked correct in every other check.
//
// `l0_text` is always defined, and the accent axis REWRITES it, so this still
// glows amber under `accent: .amber` and cyan under `.cyan` — the composition
// survives, and the standalone case stops being silently dead.
let l0_shadow_ink  = l0_text
let l0_shadow_blur = 22
let l0_shadow_dx   = 0
let l0_shadow_dy   = 0
